  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "q4tqNtBe+o5XyJK3xfP9manUIn0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:33:32.867Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Redirect by default, in-page by config\n\nBy default Connect authenticates by **redirecting** the user to the Renown portal to connect a wallet and mint the credential, then returning to the app. In-page sign-in \u2014 pick a login method inside Connect, sign the credential there, written and logged in via Switchboard without leaving the app \u2014 is opt-in and configured entirely through `powerhouse.config.json`.\n\n- **`connect.renown.switchboardUrl`** \u2014 the Switchboard GraphQL endpoint. When set, Connect *attempts* in-page sign-in. When absent, or when no wallet session can be produced, Connect falls back to the redirect flow automatically, so nothing breaks if it is left unset.\n- **`connect.renown.adapters`** \u2014 presence of a key enables that adapter.\n\n```json\n\"renown\": {\n  \"url\": \"https://www.renown.id\",\n  \"switchboardUrl\": \"https://switchboard.example/graphql\",\n  \"adapters\": {\n    \"rainbow\": { \"walletConnectProjectId\": \"...\" },\n    \"privy\": { \"appId\": \"...\", \"methods\": [\"google\", \"email\"] }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## The two adapters\n\n**`rainbow`** (`{ walletConnectProjectId }`) \u2014 external wallets via RainbowKit + wagmi. Treat `walletConnectProjectId` as **required in practice**: without it only an installed browser wallet (or a Safe App iframe) can sign in, because every other RainbowKit wallet connects over the WalletConnect relay, which needs a project id. Those wallets are omitted rather than offered and failing.\n\n**`privy`** (`{ appId, clientId?, methods? }`) \u2014 embedded wallets plus social/email login. `methods` defaults to `[\"google\", \"email\"]`. Social and email login run inside Privy's own modal, with OAuth in a popup so the page stays alive. Each method must be enabled in the Privy dashboard with Connect's origin allowlisted.\n\n## Two operational notes\n\nOnly **public** identifiers belong in the config \u2014 a Privy **App Secret** is server-only and must never appear in `powerhouse.config.json`. And each adapter's wallet library is fetched only on the first login click, so enabling in-page auth adds nothing to startup cost; Connect ships with every adapter's peer dependencies installed, so operators only edit config.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/07-Authorization/01-RenownAuthenticationFlow.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:33:32.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:33:32.867Z"
    }
  },
